{
  "headline": "Insulin glargine is not on FDA's shortage list; supply traces to plants with VAI and OAI history but no recent action before today",
  "headline_cites": ["D4", "E5", "E15", "E7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's drug shortage list shows insulin glargine is not listed as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label (SPL set 99ea856d) names Genzyme Corporation (FEI 3009389940) as a registered plant for labeling and packing, last inspected NAI on 2025-08-14.",
      "cites": ["E5"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same label names Sanofi-Aventis Deutschland GmbH (FEI 3003195501) as a registered plant for analysis, labeling, manufacture, and packing, last inspected VAI on 2022-03-25.",
      "cites": ["E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection records for Sanofi-Aventis Deutschland GmbH include an OAI classification on 2010-09-16 (known 2010-12-15) and a Warning Letter on 2011-02-08, with subsequent inspections all VAI through 2022-03-25.",
      "cites": ["E7", "E14", "E13"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No FDA regulatory action or shortage posting is recorded for these plants before today's date.",
      "cites": ["D4", "E5", "E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 94 syringes (7.4 days on hand at 12.6/day); Corvale Lakeside holds 70 syringes (26.5 days on hand at 2.6/day).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 33 syringes of 1.5 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would leave Lakeside with 14 days and bring East to 10 days.",
      "cites": ["D5"]
    }
  ]
}
